ZMK's app/src/split/bluetooth/central.c with Defy's split scanning recovery.

zmk_split_central.cmake checks that ZMK's file has the SHA-256 below, copies
it into the build directory and applies this patch with git apply, which
refuses any hunk that does not match exactly. A ZMK update that changes the
file stops the build until this patch is reviewed against it. Every change
but the <zephyr/sys/atomic.h> include and the retry_scanning() call is marked
"Defy:" in the patched file; docs/ble-input-recovery.md explains them.

